A plain launch never shows Tolkara's library, its execution mode chooser or Diagnostics.

Joe, 2026-11-19: screens that are Tolkara's own, not Brighter Pocket's, should not reach a player.
With no way to run the game (the setup recorded no execution mode, or one this build cannot use),
a plain launch showed the app library (with its + to add an app and its Execution Mode button) and
the mode chooser; it now says on the loading screen that Pocket needs setting up again from the
Mac. When a start stops, the loading screen's Diagnostics button (Tolkara's runtime probes and
session-ending tests) shows only in development runs; Details and Logs stay. Development runs
(launches with arguments, tools/) keep everything.
Upstream note: Brighter Pocket's own: Tolkara is a library of apps with a player who chooses.

